module test.fixture.decl_facts_reflection.witness_support


// Single authority: specimen rows, duplicate_qn oracle (both roots), dimensionless positive-control deps.
//
// `dag/std` is deliberately NOT a root, and its absence is load-bearing rather than an omission.
// `decl_facts` is a parse-only corpus walk: the pool decides which declarations become facts, and
// nothing more. The resolved half of a projection — resolved variant name, parent qualified name —
// is not read from the pool at all; `marshal_data_initializer_projection_for_item` resolves through
// `typed_module_for_path`, i.e. the prepared scope, which carries std whatever this list says. So a
// std root bought no resolution and no fact any row looks up: every qualified name the consuming
// witnesses name is a fixture path or `extdeps.units.dimensionless`, never a std declaration.
//
// What it cost was the whole scan. std is 1,298,751 of the 1,311,432 bytes these roots reach (99.0%,
// 138 of 152 files), and the required floor builds a fresh `InterpContext` per CLAIM, so the scan is
// paid once per ROW rather than once per module — 28 rows, 28 whole-std parses.
// A ROOT THAT NO LITERAL NAMES IS NOT AN UNREAD ROOT, and the counterexample is in this very
// list. A static scan for qualified-name literals reports the duplicate_qn SHADOW root below as
// unread: no row spells a name under it. It is read. The rows reach it through pool AMBIGUITY --
// the shadow declares the same qualified name as the primary, and what the witnesses assert is
// that the lookup returns BOTH candidates -- so the root is named by nothing and load-bearing
// anyway. Executed rather than reasoned: deleting the shadow root reds
// decl_fact_lookup_duplicate_qualified_identity_returns_ambiguous_both_candidates and
// decl_facts_duplicate_qn_pool_declaration_lookup_per_candidate_is_unique.
//
// So a census over pool roots produces CANDIDATES, never a removal list. What decides is the
// mutation battery, run under BOTH root sets with the red sets compared at IDENTITY grain: a
// count match is not a match. Removing a root that is merely unnamed makes the rows over it pass
// vacuously -- cheaper AND unfalsifiable, which is worse than the cost it saved.
//
// INERT ROOT, FOUND THEN REMOVED (census 2026-08-18, report-first): dag/extdeps/external_authority
// contributed ZERO files. The module is the FILE dag/extdeps/external_authority.dag, and
// corpus_dag_files_for_roots walks a root only `if root_path.is_dir()`, so a root naming a file was
// skipped in silence -- no diagnostic, no count, no refusal. The row it was meant to serve
// (decl_facts_reflection_imported_external_authority_positive_control) passes regardless, because
// the parent qualified name it asserts comes from RESOLUTION through the prepared scope, not from
// this pool. It was the only such root among the 41 pool-walk root literals in the corpus, and it
// is gone: it served as the positive control for the zero-contributing-root refusal, red on the
// gate landing and green on this removal.
data decl_facts_reflection_fixture_pool_roots: List<String> = [
  "dag/test/fixture/decl_facts_reflection",
  "dag/test/fixture/decl_facts_reflection_duplicate_qn/primary",
  "test/fixture_roots/decl_facts_reflection_duplicate_qn/shadow",
  "dag/extdeps/units",
]

// Skeleton outer-constructor lexeme witnesses need only parse-tree facts under specimens/;
// narrower than decl_facts_reflection_fixture_pool_roots — no duplicate_qn shadow or std closure.
data decl_facts_skeleton_fixture_pool_roots: List<String> = [
  "dag/test/fixture/decl_facts_reflection",
]

data decl_facts_reflection_fixture_facts: List<v2.std.decl_index.DeclFact> = v2.std.decl_index.decl_facts(pool_roots: decl_facts_reflection_fixture_pool_roots)

data decl_facts_skeleton_fixture_facts: List<v2.std.decl_index.DeclFact> = v2.std.decl_index.decl_facts(pool_roots: decl_facts_skeleton_fixture_pool_roots)

fn decl_fact_skeleton_for_qualified_name(
  facts: List<v2.std.decl_index.DeclFact>,
  qn: String
) -> Node? {
  v2.std.decl_facts_skeleton.decl_fact_skeleton_for_resolution(
    resolution: v2.std.decl_facts_skeleton.resolve_decl_fact_by_qualified_name(facts: facts, qn: qn)
  )
}
